  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"9a\"><p><strong>9a</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>Electric field strength at a point is the force per unit charge experienced by a small positive point (test) charge placed at that point.</p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"9b\"><p><strong>9b</strong></p><p></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\left ( 8.99 \\times 10^{9} \\right )\\left ( 2 \\times 1.6 \\times 10^{-19} \\right )}{x^{2}} = \\frac{\\left ( 8.99 \\times 10^{9} \\right )\\left ( 0.013 \\times 10^{-15} \\right )}{\\left ( 3.8-x \\right )^{2}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x \\approx 0.52\"></span> m</p>\n<p></p></section>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The distance between an alpha-particle and a point charge of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"+0.013\"></span> fC is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3.8\"></span> m. M is a point on the straight line connecting the alpha-particle and the point charge. The distance between the alpha-particle and M is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x\"></span>.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>The electric field strength at M is zero.</p>\n<p>a. Outline what is meant by electric field strength.</p>\n<p>   [2]</p>\n<p>b. Find <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x\"></span>.</p>\n<p>   [3]</p>"
  },
